A relative `--target` resolves against the workdir and replaces the machine's declared `artifact:`
for the whole report. The declared `index.md` is seeded at a different status, so the reported one
can only have come from the target.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-run
title: Run
summary: Single-machine fixture for playbook-state.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  intake: []
  research: [intake]

states:
  main:
    artifact: index.md
    initial: intaking
    statuses:
      intaking:
        transitions:
          - to: researching
            when: intake complete
            gates: ["request captured in the artifact"]
          - to: parked
            when: the run is shelved
      researching:
        transitions:
          - to: done
            when: research complete
      parked: {terminal: true}
      done: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/intake/prompt.md --
---
summary: Intake the request.
---

Intake body.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-run/research/prompt.md --
---
summary: Research the request.
---

Research body.
-- fixtures/cwd/run/index.md --
---
status: intaking
---

Body.
-- fixtures/cwd/run/review.md --
---
status: researching
---

Body.
-- cmd --
booping playbook-state fx-run --workdir run --target review.md
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
playbook: fx-run
workdir: {CWD}/run
states:
  main:
    artifact: {CWD}/run/review.md
    status: researching
    next:
    - to: done
      when: research complete
